            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="WEL01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Arthur</forename>
                        <surname>Wellesley</surname>
                        <addName>Wesley, first duke of Wellington</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1769-05-01">
                        <placeName>Ireland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1852-09-14"/>
                    <occupation>army officer</occupation>
                    <occupation>prime minister</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>All but two of Godwin's entries relate to public events, and those two 
    are when he writes to Wellington, and when he receives a reply.</p>
                        <p>That the letter to and reply from Wellington do
    indeed refer to the Duke is confirmed by Marshall, p. 384, describing the aftermath of the fire in 
    the Houses of Parliament: Godwin 'immediately wrote to the Duke of Wellington, who said that he 
    would look into the matter' (Marshall, p. 384). The letter is not in Abinger.
</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Marshall.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
